<h1>2. Visual Style &#8212; SNES / 16-bit Retro</h1>

<h2>2.1 Aesthetic Direction</h2>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-bottom:6.0pt'>The entire game uses a
SNES/early 16-bit era aesthetic. This is not a superficial filter &#8212; it
defines every visual element from UI chrome to character portraits to
animations. The style should feel like a polished SNES RPG/sports game hybr=
id:
rich enough to be expressive, pixelated enough to be unmistakably retro.</p>

